1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,630
Laddoo Lab thinks it is
healthy, honest and home-made.

2
00:00:03,930 --> 00:00:07,971
But when Zoya asked parents, one
word kept coming up: expensive.

3
00:00:08,521 --> 00:00:12,672
What a brand wants to be, and what
people think it is, are not always the

4
00:00:12,672 --> 00:00:13,572
same.

5
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:18,224
Last time, Dev gave Laddoo Lab its
name, logo, colours and tagline.

6
00:00:18,574 --> 00:00:21,718
Now Zoya wants to know: is
the message getting through?

7
00:00:22,067 --> 00:00:26,265
So she stands at the school gate with
a clipboard, and asks thirty parents

8
00:00:26,265 --> 00:00:27,545
one simple question.

9
00:00:28,195 --> 00:00:29,772
So what is the difference?

10
00:00:30,072 --> 00:00:33,342
Brand identity is how the
company wants to be seen.

11
00:00:33,342 --> 00:00:34,823
The company sends it.

12
00:00:35,173 --> 00:00:38,495
Brand image is how customers
actually see the brand.

13
00:00:38,495 --> 00:00:40,210
It lives in their minds.

14
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:45,136
Kevin Lane Keller described brand
image as the associations people hold

15
00:00:45,136 --> 00:00:47,015
in memory about a brand.

16
00:00:47,365 --> 00:00:49,495
Identity is the message sent.

17
00:00:49,495 --> 00:00:51,677
Image is the message received.

18
00:00:52,327 --> 00:00:53,983
Let's run Zoya's survey.

19
00:00:54,333 --> 00:00:58,457
Her question: what three words come
to mind when you think of Laddoo Lab?

20
00:00:58,807 --> 00:01:00,310
The answers pour in.

21
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:01,210
Healthy.

22
00:01:01,026 --> 00:01:01,926
Tasty.

23
00:01:01,642 --> 00:01:02,542
Home-made.

24
00:01:02,758 --> 00:01:04,197
But also, expensive.

25
00:01:04,197 --> 00:01:06,764
And a few say, it is for grandparents.

26
00:01:07,114 --> 00:01:11,408
Zoya counts the words, and compares
them with the identity she wanted.

27
00:01:11,758 --> 00:01:13,940
Healthy and home-made match well.

28
00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:14,873
But honest?

29
00:01:14,873 --> 00:01:16,487
Hardly anyone says it.

30
00:01:16,837 --> 00:01:19,100
And expensive is the biggest gap.

31
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:20,953
That is the image problem.

32
00:01:21,303 --> 00:01:22,715
So Laddoo Lab acts.

33
00:01:22,715 --> 00:01:26,548
The pack now shows the truth:
just twenty rupees a laddoo.

34
00:01:26,898 --> 00:01:31,762
Dev posts photos of kids sharing
cocoa-ragi at lunch, with a short note

35
00:01:31,762 --> 00:01:33,399
on what goes inside.

36
00:01:33,749 --> 00:01:36,220
Two months later, Zoya asks again.

37
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:38,795
Expensive drops, and honest goes up.

38
00:01:39,445 --> 00:01:41,328
You control your identity.

39
00:01:41,328 --> 00:01:43,316
Customers decide your image.

40
00:01:44,016 --> 00:01:48,681
Jean-Noël Kapferer, a French professor,
drew brand identity as a prism

41
00:01:48,681 --> 00:01:49,958
with six sides.

42
00:01:50,308 --> 00:01:51,900
Physique: how it looks.

43
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:54,069
The navy pack and the laddoo logo.

44
00:01:54,369 --> 00:01:56,531
Personality: if it were a person.

45
00:01:56,531 --> 00:01:58,362
Warm and honest, like Nani.

46
00:01:58,662 --> 00:02:00,368
Culture: its values.

47
00:02:00,368 --> 00:02:02,755
No shortcuts, real ingredients.

48
00:02:03,055 --> 00:02:05,434
Relationship: what it does for you.

49
00:02:05,434 --> 00:02:07,571
A helping hand on busy mornings.

50
00:02:07,871 --> 00:02:09,959
Reflection: the typical buyer.

51
00:02:09,959 --> 00:02:11,708
A busy parent who cares.

52
00:02:12,008 --> 00:02:15,065
And self-image: how buyers
feel about themselves.

53
00:02:15,065 --> 00:02:16,512
I am a good parent.

54
00:02:17,162 --> 00:02:19,129
Where do we see this at work today?

55
00:02:19,479 --> 00:02:20,379
Identity.

56
00:02:20,243 --> 00:02:23,709
A bank decides it wants to
feel modern and friendly.

57
00:02:24,059 --> 00:02:24,959
Image.

58
00:02:24,673 --> 00:02:29,071
A food delivery app reads reviews
to learn what people really think.

59
00:02:29,421 --> 00:02:30,321
The gap.

60
00:02:30,166 --> 00:02:34,542
An airline wants to feel premium,
but people talk about late flights.

61
00:02:34,892 --> 00:02:35,818
Closing it.

62
00:02:35,818 --> 00:02:39,593
A hospital shows its prices
clearly, so it feels honest.

63
00:02:40,243 --> 00:02:42,991
But can a brand simply choose its image?

64
00:02:42,991 --> 00:02:43,891
No.

65
00:02:43,804 --> 00:02:44,964
The good side.

66
00:02:44,964 --> 00:02:47,439
Listening shows exactly what to fix.

67
00:02:47,789 --> 00:02:48,973
The hard side.

68
00:02:48,973 --> 00:02:52,903
An image changes slowly, and
one bad story spreads fast.

69
00:02:53,253 --> 00:02:56,803
Dev wants to drop Nani from
the posts, to look young.

70
00:02:56,803 --> 00:02:57,851
Zoya says no.

71
00:02:57,851 --> 00:02:59,306
Nani is who we are.

72
00:02:59,656 --> 00:03:02,104
So they keep Nani, and add the kids.

73
00:03:02,104 --> 00:03:03,677
Old roots, young fans.

74
00:03:04,027 --> 00:03:09,121
In 1993, Keller wrote that a strong
brand image needs associations that

75
00:03:09,121 --> 00:03:11,830
are strong, favourable and unique.

76
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:13,080
The lesson?

77
00:03:12,973 --> 00:03:15,904
Say who you are, then
listen to what people hear.

78
00:03:16,554 --> 00:03:17,513
Quick check.

79
00:03:17,513 --> 00:03:19,739
Parents call Laddoo Lab expensive.

80
00:03:19,739 --> 00:03:22,231
Is that its identity, or its image?

81
00:03:24,131 --> 00:03:25,031
Its image!

82
00:03:24,949 --> 00:03:28,772
It is how customers see the
brand, not what the brand sends.

83
00:03:29,372 --> 00:03:30,386
So, remember.

84
00:03:30,686 --> 00:03:33,338
Brand identity is what the company sends.

85
00:03:33,688 --> 00:03:36,941
Brand image is what customers
receive and remember.

86
00:03:37,291 --> 00:03:40,872
Find the gap by listening, then
close it with honest action.

87
00:03:41,472 --> 00:03:45,605
Next time, we find out what all
this trust is worth: brand equity.
